# Minimal reproducer for the unbounded-heap defect (track D -> track A).
#
# A tail-recursive countdown. `sub(n)(1)` and `int_eq(n)(0)` each produce a
# BOXED int, and every one of those boxes is dead immediately: at any instant
# THE LIVE SET IS ONE INTEGER. The recursion is in TAIL position and the runtime
# does TCO, so the stack does not grow -- anything that grows is the HEAP.
#
# Therefore peak RSS must be FLAT in the iteration count. Measured, it is not:
#         1,000 ->   0.75 MB      1,000,000 ->  72 MB
#       100,000 ->  20 MB         2,000,000 -> 105 MB
#       250,000 ->  36 MB         5,000,000 -> 170 MB
#       500,000 ->  52 MB        45,000,000 -> 519 MB
#                               135,000,000 -> 905 MB
# The GC reclaims SOMETHING (the 135M run allocates ~3.2 GB of boxes yet peaks
# at 905 MB) but it does not hold steady.
#
# ── THE PORTABLE NUMBER: ~700,000 ITERATIONS IS THE METAL'S WHOLE BUDGET ─────
# In the small-N regime growth is essentially LINEAR at ~40 BYTES RETAINED PER
# ITERATION (500k->1M costs 20.7 MB, 1M->2M costs 33 MB). Each iteration
# allocates two boxed ints = 48 bytes, so roughly 85% of what is allocated is
# never reclaimed.
#
# On bare metal the heap starts at 68.0 MiB and the LA stack's live frames sit
# just under LA_STACK_TOP = 128 MiB, so there are ~60 MiB to consume. RSS
# crosses 60 MB between N=500,000 (52 MB) and N=1,000,000 (72 MB) -- so a metal
# LA program has a total budget of roughly SEVEN HUNDRED THOUSAND allocating
# iterations, ever, after which it overwrites its own return addresses.
#
# That cross-checks the metal observation independently: every HAL.4x compositor
# dies after ~6 s of idle polling, and 700k/6s = ~117k iterations/sec, which is
# the right order for an `inb` port read under QEMU (each is a VM exit). Two
# measurements, taken different ways, agreeing.
#
# "Six seconds" is machine-dependent; "700,000 allocating iterations" is not,
# and it is the number to predict whether any given LA program survives.
#
# THE ITERATION COUNT IS READ FROM `churn.n`, not compiled in, so ONE build
# serves every measurement point. native_codegen3's codegen is the expensive
# part (~25 s even for a program this small), and a gate that compares TWO
# workloads would otherwise pay it twice. `churn.n` must hold just the decimal
# digits with NO trailing newline: str_to_int is strict on every engine and
# halts loudly on anything else, which is the behaviour wanted here rather than
# a silently-truncated count.
glyph Z    = la f. (la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))(la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))
glyph IF   = la c. la t. la f. c(t)(f)("!")
glyph LOOP = Z(la self. la n.
    IF(int_eq(n)(0))(la _. "done")(la _. self(sub(n)(1))))
glyph MAIN = print(LOOP(str_to_int(read_file("churn.n"))))
